/-
Row 4 of the sparse Collatz certificate (eq:imt-sparse-collatz).

Regenerated from
research/workstreams/inner_design/imt_asymptotic/certify_imt_sparse.py and
cross-checked against SPARSE_EXACT.json: the SHA-256 of the residual
polynomial matches the stored coefficients_sha256 field, so this is the
certified polynomial and not a recomputation that happens to look similar.

The stored residual has an exact zero of order 1 at x = 0. This list is that
residual divided by x, then scaled by the positive LCM of its coefficient
denominators. Scaling by a positive constant preserves the sign, so the
integer list certifies the rational residual; see rat_poly_neg_of_int_scaled.

The certificate is checked by the Lean kernel via decide. Compiled
evaluation is deliberately avoided: it would enlarge the axiom closure,
which scripts/check.sh rejects.
-/
